AiTask weekly_category_revenue_week_over_week {
  label: "Weekly Category Revenue with Week-over-Week Change"
  description: "Posts last week's category revenue and week-over-week change to Slack."

  brief: @md
    1. From @Dataset:ecommerce_official, get revenue by product category for the last complete Monday–Sunday week and the preceding complete Monday–Sunday week.
    2. For every product category, calculate the percentage change in revenue versus the preceding week.
    3. Sort categories from highest to lowest revenue for the last complete week.
    4. Produce only one plain-text line per category in exactly this format: `Category: $revenue (+/-X% vs the week before)`. Use currency formatting for revenue and a signed percentage change. Do not include a headline, reporting period, explanation, total, blank line, or footer.

    Delivery: After every run, post the completed lines to the Slack channel #nhity-test.
  ;;

  acceptance_criteria: @md
    - Covers exactly the last complete Monday–Sunday week and the preceding complete Monday–Sunday week.
    - Includes every available product category exactly once, sorted from highest to lowest last-week revenue.
    - Each category appears on one plain-text line in the exact requested structure: `Category: $revenue (+/-X% vs the week before)`, with currency-formatted revenue and signed week-over-week percentage change.
    - Contains no headline, reporting period, explanation, total, blank line, or footer.
    - Posts the completed lines to #nhity-test after every run.
  ;;
}
